(a) Oil lines. Oil lines must meet CS 23.993 and must accommodate a flow of oil at a rate and pressure adequate for proper engine functioning under any normal operating conditions.
(b) Breather lines. Breather lines must be arranged so that –
  (1) Condensed water vapour or oil that might freeze and obstruct the line cannot accumulate at any point;
  (2) The breather discharge will not constitute a fire hazard if foaming occurs, or cause emitted oil to strike the pilot’s windshield;
  (3) The breather does not discharge into the engine air induction system;
  (4) For aerobatic category aeroplanes, there is no excessive loss of oil from the breather during aerobatic manoeuvres, including short periods of inverted flight; and
  (5) The breather outlet is protected against blockage by ice or foreign matter.
